// Cross-voice beam collision: the upper voice's stem-up beam must ride ABOVE a
// high note sustained in the lower voice, not sit on top of it. Voice 1 beams
// C5 eighths (stems up); voice 2 holds an A5 whole note that falls in the beam's
// path. LilyPond's Beam_collision_engraver raises the beam to clear it; before
// this fix the beam only saw its own voice and cut across the A5 notehead.
// The A5's horizontal note-column offset against voice 1's stems is handled by
// the note-collision meshing fallback: the A5 (down-stem voice) shifts LEFT so
// voice 1's stem clears it on the right, matching LilyPond.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/beam-collision-engraver.cc, lily/note-collision.cc:332-337.
octave absolute
title "Cross-voice beam collision"
part mel { clef treble }
section S {
  mel {
    voice { c'8 c' c' c' c' c' c' c' | }
    voice { a'1 | }
  }
}
form main { S }
score main "multivoice-beam-collision" { staff mel }
